{
  "name": "glosco",
  "description": "A distributed network monitoring system designed to track flow states and connection lifecycles globally across disparate network segments. It leverages low-level packet capture via libpcap to perform real-time protocol parsing and state machine tracking for TCP, UDP, and ICMP traffic. The architecture incorporates a peer-to-peer mesh synchronization layer built on Tokio to aggregate and broadcast connection events across multiple remote observation nodes.",
